- Test-only binaries, never in a release build: `viola-fake-agent` (a `[[bin]]` of the root package behind feature `fake-agent`, the stand-in `claude`; its print mode `-p <prompt>` / `--print <prompt>` writes its start receipts, fires the SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit (prompt set), Stop and SessionEnd `default` fixtures, prints `ok` on stdout and exits 0, never raw and never reading stdin — the mode `viola verify`'s print probe drives in CI; thirteen argv options (the count's rule is this list), no env, of which nine serve verify's interactive runs and their tests: `--trusted-root <DIR>` (an ancestor walk, both paths canonicalised), `--screens` (writes `Screen.modal` when untrusted, no hook fired, or `Screen.ready` when trusted, SessionStart as before: a clear, then rows joined by CRLF), `--turn-stop` (a submit fires UserPromptSubmit, then Stop, then writes `Screen.turn`), `--dialogs` (a pasted compiled dialog prompt replays its recorded `<stem>-<n>` variants in claim order: a call's PreToolUse fires first; with no decision, its PermissionRequest fires; a decision from either fires its PostToolUse), `--framing` (a pasted compiled paste text fires its recorded `paste-1` / `paste-2` / `paste-3` UserPromptSubmit variant with its bytes unchanged, a new stem reached through `ledger::framing_stem` with no option added, the probed local command fires the recorded `clear-1` SessionEnd then SessionStart and no UserPromptSubmit, and `/compact` fires the recorded `SessionStart.compact-1` with `session_id` set to the last SessionStart the agent fired (the launch one or a replayed clear's; only a SessionStart whose fixture exists moves it) and no UserPromptSubmit;
 a set without a variant fires nothing for it) and the two test-only holds `--stop-receipt-hold-ms <n>` (capped at 1 000 ms, a hold of the Stop hook's receipt that forces a race window open) and `--paste-hint-ms <ms>` (capped at 10 000 ms; with `--framing`, after the long text's replay and its Stop the screen is cleared and `Screen.turn` is drawn only after the hold), and the test-only screen switch `--tag-turn-screen <phase>` (with `--framing` and `--turn-stop`: after the turn of the compiled tag-like paste, and after no other turn, `Screen.<phase>` of the set is drawn in place of `Screen.turn`; a missing file draws nothing), and the test-only screen switch `--long-turn-screen <phase>` (with `--framing` and `--turn-stop`: after the long paste's turn alone, after its Stop, `Screen.<phase>` of the set is drawn in place of `Screen.turn`), and two serve `viola revive`'s tests and, under the fake agent, verify's Run E: `--resume <id>` (the SessionStart fired at launch is the set's recorded `SessionStart.resume-1.json` when the set holds it (`RESUME_VARIANT`, `launch_variant`; 2.1.287 since chunk 2026-10-14-resume-and-compact-ledger-rows), else its recorded `SessionStart.default` payload, with `source` set to `resume` and `session_id` set to the id given, the trailing newline kept) and `--fork-session` (beside `--resume`, `session_id` is the compiled id `0f0e0d0c-0b0a-4908-8706-050403020100`; alone it changes nothing); without `--resume` every payload is the recorded bytes; and two serve the statusline tests: `--settings <file>` and `--statusline-stdin <file>` (with both, and only when the settings file's `statusLine` command, split on ASCII white space, is an absolute command, it runs that command with the stdin file's bytes and files a `statusline` receipt, the `hook` receipt's fields without `event`);
 `--framing` with `--settings <file>` alone replays the set's recorded status line the same way, the one word exactly `"$0"` handed over as `/bin/sh`, spawned directly and never through a shell: `StatusLine.default-1.json` after the launch SessionStart's hooks and `StatusLine.rate-limits-1.json` once at the end of the first Stop's turn, after the turn screen (a relative command is receipted and never run; a set without the variants fires nothing; no option added); beside the options it takes two mode words: `statusline-echo`, which prints its output and files its stdin and exits with the code after the marker path, and `agents` (chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board), which answers `agents --json` from files beside its own executable: `agents-mode` (`recorded` · `oversize` · `malformed`, absent read as `recorded`), `agents-rows.json` (planted rows, printed unchanged) and a live `sessions/<pid>.json` registry its interactive runs write (a row written just before its launch SessionStart fires, its `cwd` the launch fixture's recorded `cwd`, `~` without one; a dead or reused pid left out through one `viola_state::liveness::start_times()` read); no option and no env are added (the founder's own answer to P4 fork 2, that chunk's `inputs#I1`)) and `viola-harness` (in `viola-e2e`, behind `scripts/agent-run.{sh,ps1}`; its command contract is test-plan §3) and `viola-mcp-tap` (a `[[bin]]` of `viola-e2e` that records a live MCP exchange for the `Mcp.` fixtures, Repository below: `record <capture> <viola exe> <args…>` is a direct spawn, no shell and no PATH lookup, each line read through `take(MAX_FRAME)` and appended once, tagged with its direction, to a capture created 0600, exiting with the child;
 `fixture <capture> <out>` keeps the client frames up to and including the first `tools/list` request and each request's result keyed by method, through `ledger::scrub` (the home → `~`, the user word → `<user>`) and then `ledger::screen_fault` over every string and key, refusing with the file name and one closed code `home-path` · `absolute-path` · `username` · `email`, never the content).
